                <h1 class="page-header" style="margin-top:15px;"></h1>
			<h3>
Withdrawal of Admission : <span style="font-size:18px;">Students are required to follow the process of cancellation outlined in the offer letter / call for counselling letter. </span>
</h3><hr/>
<!--	<p><strong><em><font color="white">Kindly note that, This Application is not Valid For NCDOE School Program. </font></em></strong></p>-->		
				

	<div>
	    
	<br />
	
	<p><strong style="font-size: 18px;">For Technical Program / Courses :</strong></p>
<p>A full refund of fees will be provided for cancellation of admission to technical&nbsp;courses / programs on or before 20th July 2026<strong>,&nbsp;</strong>as per AICTE norms.</p>
<br>
<p><strong style="font-size: 18px;">For Non-&nbsp;Technical Program / Courses :</strong></p>
<p>Refund is as per UGC refund policy 2024-25, (dated 12th June 2024, bearing the number D.O. No.F.2-7 1t2022 (CPP-Il) (c-1 14s46)) or subsequent amendment, if any.</p>
<br>
<p><b style="font-size: 18px;">Kindly refer revised UGC notification for refund policy</b> <strong><a href="https://www.ugc.gov.in/pdfnews/1654477_Fee-Refund-Policy-2024-25.pdf" 
style="color: #ffffff;font-weight: 700;font-size: large;background-color: #a12e27;padding:3px;">Click here</a></strong></p>
<br>

<p><strong style="font-size: 18px;">Cancellation policy not valid for online and distance learning program (NCDOE School)</strong></p>
<br>
	<!--<p style="">The First year candidates who have paid the fees for the academic year can withdraw the admission and be eligible for refund as per the NMIMS refund policy informed and agreed upon during the admission process.</p>-->
<p>The student who wishes to withdraw admission should fill the application form using the url <a href="https://nmims.edu/admission-cancellation"><font color="white"><b>https://nmims.edu/admission-cancellation</b></font></a> available on our website <strong>nmims.edu</strong>. Withdrawal request can be applied only through this link.</p>
<p><b style="font-size: 18px;">Request before commencement of program: </b>the admission department will process the document with the necessary approvals.</p>
<p><b style="font-size: 18px;">Request post the commencement of program:</b> the candidate will have to get the Clearance /No dues from all the concerned departments of the School.</p>
<p>Once the process is completed, the refund of the fees (if applicable) shall be processed within 15 days of submission of the completed form with associated documents. Refund of fees, if any, will be credited to the bank account details provided by the applicant in the application. If any dues are to be collected, that will be deducted before a refund of the fees.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>

<!--<p><b>Kindly refer your admission offer letter for refund policy.</b></p>-->


